      "summary": "The founding rulebook for Sweaty Dynasty v2.",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "tldr",
          "title": "TL;DR",
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "tldr-revival-drafts-we-will-start-with",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "Revival Drafts: We will start with a 3-6 asset keeper/dispersal draft. Managers can keep players and/or picks, and may later draft players and/or picks in the dispersal draft. The rookie draft will follow the dispersal draft."
            },
            {
              "id": "tldr-buy-in-50-year-partial-full",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "Buy-In: $50/year. Partial/full due must be paid in order to trade future draft picks."
            },
            {
              "id": "tldr-payouts-are-split-into-three-categories",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "Payouts are split into three categories: minigames/awards, yearly payout, and the empire rolling pot."
            },
            {
              "id": "tldr-roster-1-qb-2-rb-3",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "Roster: 1 QB, 2 RB, 3 WR, 1 TE, 3 FLX, 14 bench, 3 IR, 4 Taxi"
            },
            {
              "id": "tldr-scoring-modified-1-qb-tep-tight",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "Scoring: Modified 1 QB TEP (tight end premium). Added first down scoring and QB boosts."
            },
            {
              "id": "tldr-trading-no-vetoes-conditional-trades-are",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "Trading: No vetoes. Conditional trades are here!"
            },
            {
              "id": "tldr-waivers-faab-format-100-in-season",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "Waivers: FAAB format. $100 in-season and $100 offseason FAAB."
            },
            {
              "id": "tldr-playoffs-toilet-bowl-6-team-playoff",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "Playoffs & Toilet Bowl: 6-team playoff. 6 seed is a Points For wildcard spot. Championship side placement matchups will determine draft order. Small FAAB reward for toilet bowl 7th and 9th place winners."
            },
            {
              "id": "tldr-rookie-draft-order-tanking-true-tanking",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "Rookie Draft Order & Tanking: True tanking is allowed. Non-playoff team draft order is determined by MAX PF. Playoff team draft order determined by placement matchups."
            },
            {
              "id": "tldr-empire-scoring-format-2-titles-wins",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "Empire Scoring Format: 2 titles wins the Empire and the rolling empire pot. 1 title plus other quality finishes can also win the empire. The league will reset with a 5 asset keeper/dispersal draft."
            },
            {
              "id": "tldr-important-dates-trade-period-6-14",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "Important Dates: Trade Period: 6/14-6/20. Cutdown day: 6/21. Dispersal draft: 6/2-completion. Rookie draft: TBD"
            },
            {
              "id": "tldr-replacement-managers-if-you-must-leave",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "Replacement Managers: If you must leave the league, please help find your replacement manager. The adopting manager will keep all accumulated empire points from that team."
            },
            {
              "id": "tldr-league-end-of-life-if-managers",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "League End of Life: If managers collectively decide to end the league, the empire pot will be split among the managers, proportionate to their share of league-wide empire points."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "revival",
          "title": "Revival Drafts",
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "revival-welcome-to-sweaty-dynasty-v2-to",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "Welcome to Sweaty Dynasty v2! To revive the league from the dead, we will begin with a partial dispersal draft. Here's how it works:"
            },
            {
              "id": "revival-each-manager-must-select-between-3",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "Each manager must select between 3 and 6 assets they wish to keep. These assets may be players or draft picks."
            },
            {
              "id": "revival-to-maintain-competitive-fairness-managers-will",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "To maintain competitive fairness, managers will be required to send their keeper selections to the commissioner by the cutdown deadline."
            },
            {
              "id": "revival-if-a-manager-does-not-have",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "If a manager does not have their picks in at the deadline, the top three assets (as defined by current SF, TEP value on Keep Trade Cut) will be chosen."
            },
            {
              "id": "revival-every-player-that-is-not-selected",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "Every player that is not selected as a 'keeper' will then go back into a league-wide player pool."
            },
            {
              "id": "revival-the-league-will-then-draft-from",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "The league will then draft from the player pool as they would in a startup. Each manager will be able to draft any non-rookie player, including kickers, which will represent the non-kept rookie draft picks."
            },
            {
              "id": "revival-the-first-kicker-picked-will-represent",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "The first kicker picked will represent the first remaining (non-keeper) draft pick. If picks 1.01 through 1.08 were all selected as keeper picks by their respective managers, 1.09 would be the first available pick on the board and would be represented by the first kicker drafted."
            },
            {
              "id": "revival-the-order-of-the-draft-will",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "The order of the draft will be determined randomly after the keeper selections have been made. This will be a linear draft."
            },
            {
              "id": "revival-managers-that-keep-only-3-assets",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "Managers that keep only 3 assets will begin drafting in the 1st round. Managers that keep 4, 5, and 6 players will forego their 1st, 1st and 2nd, and 1st 2nd and 3rd round picks, respectively. As picks can't be 'cancelled', managers will be asked to select a non-relevant player (retired, defense, etc.) as a dummy pick."
            },
            {
              "id": "revival-after-the-dispersal-draft-we-will",
              "depth": 0,
              "text": "After the dispersal draft, we will do a full rookie draft based on the picks kept by managers and kickers drafted in the dispersal draft."
            }
          ]
        },
